   "file": "02-operation.md",
   "group": "Section 2 · Operation",
   "level": 3,
   "boards": [],
   "html": "<p>Photograph of the 732A front panel with numbered callout balloons 1-15 leading to specific features. Panel legend reads \"FLUKE 732A DC REFERENCE STANDARD\" at upper left. Visible printed labels on the panel, top row (near callouts 1, 2, 3): \"1.018V\", \"1V\", \"10V\" (small calibration-tool adjustment holes below the LED display strip). Upper right LED column, top to bottom: \"AC PWR\", \"BTRY CHG\", \"IN CAL\", and below them \"RESET\". Lower panel binding posts, left to right as labeled on the panel: \"1.018V HI\", \"10V HI\", \"LO\", \"LO\", \"1V HI\", \"CHASSIS GROUND\", \"GUARD\" (marked \"⏚ ←60V MAX→\" between the CHASSIS GROUND and GUARD posts), and at far left two posts labeled \"OVEN TEMP THERMISTOR\". Below the OVEN TEMP THERMISTOR posts is the symbol for floating terminals with the note \"ALL FLOATING TERMINALS 60V MAX\".<\/p>\n<p>Callout numbers 1-15 correspond to Table 2-1 items (see below): 1 = 1.018V Adjustment (small hole under \"1.018V\" legend), 2 = 1V Adjustment (small hole under \"1V\" legend), 3 = 10V Adjustment (small hole under \"10V\" legend), 4 = AC PWR indicator, 5 = BTRY CHG indicator, 6 = IN CAL indicator, 7 = RESET, 8 = GUARD terminal, 9 = CHASSIS GROUND terminal, 10 = 1V HI terminal, 11 = LO terminal (10V common), 12 = LO terminal (1V/1.018V common), 13 = 10V HI terminal, 14 = 1.018V HI terminal, 15 = OVEN TEMP THERMISTOR terminals (pair).<\/p>",
   "text": "Photograph of the 732A front panel with numbered callout balloons 1-15 leading to specific features. Panel legend reads \"FLUKE 732A DC REFERENCE STANDARD\" at upper left. Visible printed labels on the panel, top row (near callouts 1, 2, 3): \"1.018V\", \"1V\", \"10V\" (small calibration-tool adjustment holes below the LED display strip). Upper right LED column, top to bottom: \"AC PWR\", \"BTRY CHG\", \"IN CAL\", and below them \"RESET\". Lower panel binding posts, left to right as labeled on the panel: \"1.018V HI\", \"10V HI\", \"LO\", \"LO\", \"1V HI\", \"CHASSIS GROUND\", \"GUARD\" (marked \"⏚ ←60V MAX→\" between the CHASSIS GROUND and GUARD posts), and at far left two posts labeled \"OVEN TEMP THERMISTOR\". Below the OVEN TEMP THERMISTOR posts is the symbol for floating terminals with the note \"ALL FLOATING TERMINALS 60V MAX\". Callout numbers 1-15 correspond to Table 2-1 items (see below): 1 = 1.018V Adjustment (small hole under \"1.018V\" legend), 2 = 1V Adjustment (small hole under \"1V\" legend), 3 = 10V Adjustment (small hole under \"10V\" legend), 4 = AC PWR indicator, 5 = BTRY CHG indicator, 6 = IN CAL indicator, 7 = RESET, 8 = GUARD terminal, 9 = CHASSIS GROUND terminal, 10 = 1V HI terminal, 11 = LO terminal (10V common), 12 = LO terminal (1V/1.018V common), 13 = 10V HI terminal, 14 = 1.018V HI terminal, 15 = OVEN TEMP THERMISTOR terminals (pair).",
