   "level": 3,
   "boards": [],
   "html": "<p>Photograph of the 732A rear panel, divided into two modules (AC Module at left, Battery Module at right), with numbered callout balloons 1-8.<\/p>\n<p>Left module (AC Module) printed text: a serial number label reading \"S/N 3030016\" near callout 1. \"WARNING / PANEL MOUNTING SCREWS REQUIRED FOR CHASSIS GROUNDING.\" \"WARNING / GROUNDING CONDUCTOR IN POWER CORD MUST BE CONNECTED TO INSURE PROTECTION FROM ELECTRIC SHOCK.\" \"SUPPLY SETTING / 90-132V AC ☐ 50-60Hz / 200-264V AC ☐ 30VA\". \"CAUTION / FOR FIRE PROTECTION REPLACE ONLY WITH A 250V FUSE OF THE INDICATED VALUE. / 90-132V 3/8A SB / 200-264V 3/16A SB\". Below, the IEC power connector and fuse holder, and a plate reading \"JOHN FLUKE MFG. CO., INC. / EVERETT, WASHINGTON / MADE IN U.S.A.\"<\/p>\n<p>Right module (Battery Module) printed text: \"BATTERY OPR / OFF ON\" above the slide switch and its indicator lamp. \"POWER INPUT / + −\" above the two banana jacks, with \"24-40V DC / OR / 24-30V AC / 50-60Hz / 0.5A\" printed below the jacks. \"CAUTION / TO PREVENT INSTRUMENT DAMAGE DO NOT CONNECT TO ANY FRONT PANEL CONNECTORS. USE FLOATING SOURCE ONLY.\" A plate reading \"JOHN FLUKE MFG. CO., INC. / EVERETT, WASHINGTON / MADE IN U.S.A.\"<\/p>\n<p>Callout numbers 1-8 correspond to Table 2-2 items (see below): 1 = AC Module, 2 = Battery Module, 3 = SUPPLY SETTING label, 4 = chassis ground terminal (⏚ symbol), 5 = BATTERY OPR switch, 6 = POWER INPUT jacks (+ and −), 7 = Fuse holder, 8 = Power connector (IEC receptacle).<\/p>",
   "text": "Photograph of the 732A rear panel, divided into two modules (AC Module at left, Battery Module at right), with numbered callout balloons 1-8. Left module (AC Module) printed text: a serial number label reading \"S/N 3030016\" near callout 1. \"WARNING / PANEL MOUNTING SCREWS REQUIRED FOR CHASSIS GROUNDING.\" \"WARNING / GROUNDING CONDUCTOR IN POWER CORD MUST BE CONNECTED TO INSURE PROTECTION FROM ELECTRIC SHOCK.\" \"SUPPLY SETTING / 90-132V AC ☐ 50-60Hz / 200-264V AC ☐ 30VA\". \"CAUTION / FOR FIRE PROTECTION REPLACE ONLY WITH A 250V FUSE OF THE INDICATED VALUE. / 90-132V 3/8A SB / 200-264V 3/16A SB\". Below, the IEC power connector and fuse holder, and a plate reading \"JOHN FLUKE MFG. CO., INC. / EVERETT, WASHINGTON / MADE IN U.S.A.\" Right module (Battery Module) printed text: \"BATTERY OPR / OFF ON\" above the slide switch and its indicator lamp. \"POWER INPUT / + −\" above the two banana jacks, with \"24-40V DC / OR / 24-30V AC / 50-60Hz / 0.5A\" printed below the jacks. \"CAUTION / TO PREVENT INSTRUMENT DAMAGE DO NOT CONNECT TO ANY FRONT PANEL CONNECTORS. USE FLOATING SOURCE ONLY.\" A plate reading \"JOHN FLUKE MFG. CO., INC. / EVERETT, WASHINGTON / MADE IN U.S.A.\" Callout numbers 1-8 correspond to Table 2-2 items (see below): 1 = AC Module, 2 = Battery Module, 3 = SUPPLY SETTING label, 4 = chassis ground terminal (⏚ symbol), 5 = BATTERY OPR switch, 6 = POWER INPUT jacks (+ and −), 7 = Fuse holder, 8 = Power connector (IEC receptacle).",
   "mentions": []
