   "html": "<p>Four panels: <strong>ADJUSTABLE SOURCE<\/strong>, <strong>PRECISION DIVIDER<\/strong>, <strong>NULL DETECTOR<\/strong>, <strong>732A UUT<\/strong>.<\/p>\n<ul><li><strong>ADJUSTABLE SOURCE<\/strong>: terminals <strong>HI<\/strong>, <strong>SENSE +<\/strong>, <strong>SENSE −<\/strong>, <strong>LO<\/strong>, <strong>GRD<\/strong>, <strong>GND<\/strong>, wired as in Figure 4-7 (HI/SENSE+ to Precision Divider 1.0, 1.1 left unconnected; GND to Null Detector GRD and to the twisted-pair loop on the Precision Divider output leads).<\/li><li><strong>PRECISION DIVIDER<\/strong>: input terminals <strong>1.1<\/strong>, <strong>1.0<\/strong>, <strong>LO<\/strong>, <strong>GND<\/strong>; ratio shown as <strong>0.1018000 (0.1000000)<\/strong>. A second terminal cluster (<strong>HI<\/strong>, <strong>LO<\/strong>, <strong>GND<\/strong>) inside the box at its right side has its HI wired (through a twisted-pair loop symbol) to Null Detector <strong>HI<\/strong>, its LO wired along the bottom of the figure to the UUT middle-row <strong>LO<\/strong> terminal, and its GND left unwired.<\/li><li><strong>NULL DETECTOR<\/strong>: terminals <strong>HI<\/strong>, <strong>LO<\/strong>, <strong>GRD<\/strong> (the HI and LO leads pass through a twisted-pair loop symbol).<\/li><li><strong>732A UUT<\/strong>: binding posts, top row <strong>10V<\/strong>, <strong>LO<\/strong>; middle row <strong>1.018V<\/strong>, <strong>LO<\/strong>, <strong>1V<\/strong>; bottom row <strong>GND<\/strong>, <strong>GRD<\/strong>. Null Detector LO wired (through a twisted-pair loop symbol) to the UUT <strong>1.018V<\/strong> terminal; UUT middle-row <strong>LO<\/strong> wired to the Precision Divider output LO; UUT GRD wired to the twisted-pair loop (junction dot) on the UUT leads; UUT 10V, top-row LO and GND have no wires.<\/li><\/ul>\n<p><strong>NOTE: MOVE 1.018V ON UUT TO 1V FOR 1V CALIBRATION.<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>[transcriber note: no jumpers or A7 Calibration PCB references (jumper names / ppm values) appear anywhere in the text or figures on PDF pages 32-37; this section covers §4-29(partial)/4-30 through 4-40 and does not reach the A7 board adjustment procedure, which appears to be described later in Section 4]<\/p>",
   "text": "Four panels: ADJUSTABLE SOURCE, PRECISION DIVIDER, NULL DETECTOR, 732A UUT. ADJUSTABLE SOURCE: terminals HI, SENSE +, SENSE −, LO, GRD, GND, wired as in Figure 4-7 (HI/SENSE+ to Precision Divider 1.0, 1.1 left unconnected; GND to Null Detector GRD and to the twisted-pair loop on the Precision Divider output leads). PRECISION DIVIDER: input terminals 1.1, 1.0, LO, GND; ratio shown as 0.1018000 (0.1000000). A second terminal cluster (HI, LO, GND) inside the box at its right side has its HI wired (through a twisted-pair loop symbol) to Null Detector HI, its LO wired along the bottom of the figure to the UUT middle-row LO terminal, and its GND left unwired. NULL DETECTOR: terminals HI, LO, GRD (the HI and LO leads pass through a twisted-pair loop symbol). 732A UUT: binding posts, top row 10V, LO; middle row 1.018V, LO, 1V; bottom row GND, GRD. Null Detector LO wired (through a twisted-pair loop symbol) to the UUT 1.018V terminal; UUT middle-row LO wired to the Precision Divider output LO; UUT GRD wired to the twisted-pair loop (junction dot) on the UUT leads; UUT 10V, top-row LO and GND have no wires. NOTE: MOVE 1.018V ON UUT TO 1V FOR 1V CALIBRATION. [transcriber note: no jumpers or A7 Calibration PCB references (jumper names / ppm values) appear anywhere in the text or figures on PDF pages 32-37; this section covers §4-29(partial)/4-30 through 4-40 and does not reach the A7 board adjustment procedure, which appears to be described later in Section 4]",
   "mentions": []
