   "html": "<p>Exploded view of the front panel (MP34) and associated hardware, plus three wiring/component-placement details.<\/p>\n<p>Main exploded view callouts:<\/p>\n<ul><li>MP34 — leader to the large front-panel casting.<\/li><li>E6 (1) BLUE, E7 (1) GREEN — leaders to two knurled binding-post shafts at upper left.<\/li><li>E1, E2, E3, E4, E5 (See Detail I) — leader into a dashed oval enclosing 5 holes on the panel, labelled (top to bottom) RED, BLK, RED, BLK, RED — i.e. RED x3 (E1,E2,E3) and BLK x2 (E4,E5).<\/li><li>E8, E9 (See Detail II) — leader to a second, adjoining dashed circle at the right edge of the E1-E5 oval, enclosing two holes both labelled WHT.<\/li><li>MP45 (See Details I and III) — leader to a small terminal-strip bracket at right of panel.<\/li><li>MP52 — leader to a cable tie next to MP45.<\/li><li>H17(2) — leader to a washer stack below the panel.<\/li><li>H15(7) — leader to a washer/nut assembly below H17.<\/li><li>A1 — leader to the LED PCB, shown at right with ribbon cable \"From A2\" running into it; the board face carries the handwritten label \"CKT 1\".<\/li><li>H16(2) — leader to a washer at the A1 board.<\/li><li>H20(2) — leader to a nut below H16.<\/li><li>Labels cast/printed on the panel face (inside dashed circles): BLU, GRN near the two lower mounting holes at left; RED, BLK, RED, BLK, RED (top to bottom) in the E1-E5 oval; WHT, WHT in the adjoining E8/E9 circle.<\/li><\/ul>\n<p>DETAIL I — CABLE HOOKUP (See Detail III For Component Placement). NOTE: Wire Numbers Correspond To W1.<\/p>\n<ul><li>Shows a ring-tongue terminal with wire-number flags \"36\", \"27\", \"26\" and leader text \"BLACK E4,E5\".<\/li><li>W3 — leader to the cable bundle entering the MP45 terminal strip.<\/li><li>MP45 (REF) — leader to the terminal strip body.<\/li><li>Wire-number flags visible along the strip: 26 and 27 (both on the wires to the BLK terminal in the upper dashed circle), a flag at the top of the strip above the BLK terminal read as \"28\" [unclear], a flag on the loose RED terminal at left below W3 read as \"35\" [unclear], 2 (pointer-shaped flag, on the wire to the loose BLK terminal, with a small illegible square flag just above it), a small flag on the strip near its right end read as \"23\" [unclear], 33 and 24 (both on the RED terminal in the dashed circle), and a further flag on that same RED terminal read as \"29\" (verified by close zoom); wire-color labels BLK and RED mark the terminal ends.<\/li><li>A leader from the strip points right to a separate ring-tongue terminal labelled \"RED  E1, E2, E3\" carrying three wire-number flags: \"25\" and \"24\" (both verified by close zoom) and a third flag that appears to read \"33\" [unclear].<\/li><li>A separate loose ring terminal below is labelled \"RED\", with wire-number flag \"34\".<\/li><\/ul>\n<p>DETAIL II<\/p>\n<ul><li>E8, E9 — leaders to two ring-tongue terminals labelled WHT (white) at top.<\/li><li>W4 — leader to the twisted-pair cable, labelled GRA, GRA (gray) leading to \"To A5\".<\/li><\/ul>\n<p>DETAIL III — COMPONENT PLACEMENT<\/p>\n<ul><li>CR1 — leader to a diode on the small terminal-strip bracket (terminal numbers 1, 2, 3, 4 marked on the bracket; \"+\" marked near terminal 2).<\/li><li>MP45 (REF) — leader to the bracket itself.<\/li><li>R1 — leader to the resistor at the right end of the bracket.<\/li><li>C1 — leader to the tantalum capacitor body (leftmost component).<\/li><li>DS1 — leader to the neon lamp.<\/li><li>RV1 — leader to the varistor.<\/li><li>Sheet label at lower right: \"732A T&amp;B (1 of 4)\".<\/li><\/ul>\n<p>Caption: Figure 5-1. 732A Final Assembly<\/p>",
   "text": "Exploded view of the front panel (MP34) and associated hardware, plus three wiring/component-placement details. Main exploded view callouts: MP34 — leader to the large front-panel casting. E6 (1) BLUE, E7 (1) GREEN — leaders to two knurled binding-post shafts at upper left. E1, E2, E3, E4, E5 (See Detail I) — leader into a dashed oval enclosing 5 holes on the panel, labelled (top to bottom) RED, BLK, RED, BLK, RED — i.e. RED x3 (E1,E2,E3) and BLK x2 (E4,E5). E8, E9 (See Detail II) — leader to a second, adjoining dashed circle at the right edge of the E1-E5 oval, enclosing two holes both labelled WHT. MP45 (See Details I and III) — leader to a small terminal-strip bracket at right of panel. MP52 — leader to a cable tie next to MP45. H17(2) — leader to a washer stack below the panel. H15(7) — leader to a washer/nut assembly below H17. A1 — leader to the LED PCB, shown at right with ribbon cable \"From A2\" running into it; the board face carries the handwritten label \"CKT 1\". H16(2) — leader to a washer at the A1 board. H20(2) — leader to a nut below H16. Labels cast/printed on the panel face (inside dashed circles): BLU, GRN near the two lower mounting holes at left; RED, BLK, RED, BLK, RED (top to bottom) in the E1-E5 oval; WHT, WHT in the adjoining E8/E9 circle. DETAIL I — CABLE HOOKUP (See Detail III For Component Placement). NOTE: Wire Numbers Correspond To W1. Shows a ring-tongue terminal with wire-number flags \"36\", \"27\", \"26\" and leader text \"BLACK E4,E5\". W3 — leader to the cable bundle entering the MP45 terminal strip. MP45 (REF) — leader to the terminal strip body. Wire-number flags visible along the strip: 26 and 27 (both on the wires to the BLK terminal in the upper dashed circle), a flag at the top of the strip above the BLK terminal read as \"28\" [unclear], a flag on the loose RED terminal at left below W3 read as \"35\" [unclear], 2 (pointer-shaped flag, on the wire to the loose BLK terminal, with a small illegible square flag just above it), a small flag on the strip near its right end read as \"23\" [unclear], 33 and 24 (both on the RED terminal in the dashed circle), and a further flag on that same RED terminal read as \"29\" (verified by close zoom); wire-color labels BLK and RED mark the terminal ends. A leader from the strip points right to a separate ring-tongue terminal labelled \"RED E1, E2, E3\" carrying three wire-number flags: \"25\" and \"24\" (both verified by close zoom) and a third flag that appears to read \"33\" [unclear]. A separate loose ring terminal below is labelled \"RED\", with wire-number flag \"34\". DETAIL II E8, E9 — leaders to two ring-tongue terminals labelled WHT (white) at top. W4 — leader to the twisted-pair cable, labelled GRA, GRA (gray) leading to \"To A5\". DETAIL III — COMPONENT PLACEMENT CR1 — leader to a diode on the small terminal-strip bracket (terminal numbers 1, 2, 3, 4 marked on the bracket; \"+\" marked near terminal 2). MP45 (REF) — leader to the bracket itself. R1 — leader to the resistor at the right end of the bracket. C1 — leader to the tantalum capacitor body (leftmost component). DS1 — leader to the neon lamp. RV1 — leader to the varistor. Sheet label at lower right: \"732A T&B (1 of 4)\". Caption: Figure 5-1. 732A Final Assembly",
