   "file": "05-parts-a6-a7.md",
   "group": "Section 5 · Parts, A5 figure, A6 and A7",
   "level": 3,
   "boards": [
    "A6"
   ],
   "html": "<p>Two-part figure. Drawing number 732A-1604 (upper inset) and 732A-4004 (main isometric view). Page header \"732A\" top right; caption \"Figure 5-7. A6 Battery Module PCB Assembly\" centered below figure; page number \"5-23\" bottom right.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Upper inset (PCB component-side view, callout drawing 732A-1604):<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul><li>\"P4\" — connector label, upper left corner of the small board outline<\/li><li>J1, J2, J3, J4 — four connector positions shown as rectangular header outlines<\/li><li>DS1 — lamp, shown as a rectangular outline at right end of the board<\/li><li>CR1 — diode symbol below/between J4 and DS1, boxed<\/li><li>R1 — resistor symbol below CR1, boxed<\/li><li>RT2, RT1 — two small square thermistor symbols below J2/J3, left to right RT2 then RT1<\/li><\/ul>\n<p><strong>Main isometric assembly view (drawing 732A-4004):<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul><li>MP1 — battery enclosure, front end (upper left, pointing to front panel)<\/li><li>MP3 — battery enclosure, top (pointing to top cover)<\/li><li>E4, E3, E1, E2 — terminal/eyelet callouts on the A6 board edge (E4 upper left, E3 and E1 mid-board, E2 lower, right of E3)<\/li><li>A6 — pointing to the battery module PCB itself (mounted along the top/rear edge)<\/li><li>MP7 — battery enclosure, outboard side (right side panel)<\/li><li>H5(6) — six of item H5 (screw, FHP, undercut, 6-32 x 1/4), called out near MP7<\/li><li>H3 — screw, PHP, 4-24 x 3/8, pointing to a small standoff near top right<\/li><li>MP8 — jack, nylon, banana type, red<\/li><li>MP9(3) — three of item MP9 (jack, nylon, banana type, black)<\/li><li>MP10 — handle, aluminum, black, 6-32 (bottom right panel)<\/li><li>H7(2) — two of item H7 (washer, plastic, #8)<\/li><li>H6(2) — two of item H6 (screw, PHP, 6-32 x 3/8)<\/li><li>MP4 — battery enclosure, bottom (lower left)<\/li><li>BT1-BT4(4) — four gel-cell batteries, shown side by side in the main body of the assembly<\/li><li>MP2 — battery enclosure, rear end<\/li><li>H4(12) — twelve of item H4 (screw, PHP, 6-32 x 1/4)<\/li><li>H1(4) — four of item H1 (nut, insulator)<\/li><li>MP6 — battery panel w/switch (front panel, lower right, with switch and jacks mounted)<\/li><li>H2(4) — four of item H2 (screw, thread forming), lower right edge, shown with a screw symbol<\/li><\/ul>\n<p>Drawing numbers: 732A-1604 (inset), 732A-4004 (main view)<\/p>",
   "text": "Two-part figure. Drawing number 732A-1604 (upper inset) and 732A-4004 (main isometric view). Page header \"732A\" top right; caption \"Figure 5-7. A6 Battery Module PCB Assembly\" centered below figure; page number \"5-23\" bottom right. Upper inset (PCB component-side view, callout drawing 732A-1604): \"P4\" — connector label, upper left corner of the small board outline J1, J2, J3, J4 — four connector positions shown as rectangular header outlines DS1 — lamp, shown as a rectangular outline at right end of the board CR1 — diode symbol below/between J4 and DS1, boxed R1 — resistor symbol below CR1, boxed RT2, RT1 — two small square thermistor symbols below J2/J3, left to right RT2 then RT1 Main isometric assembly view (drawing 732A-4004): MP1 — battery enclosure, front end (upper left, pointing to front panel) MP3 — battery enclosure, top (pointing to top cover) E4, E3, E1, E2 — terminal/eyelet callouts on the A6 board edge (E4 upper left, E3 and E1 mid-board, E2 lower, right of E3) A6 — pointing to the battery module PCB itself (mounted along the top/rear edge) MP7 — battery enclosure, outboard side (right side panel) H5(6) — six of item H5 (screw, FHP, undercut, 6-32 x 1/4), called out near MP7 H3 — screw, PHP, 4-24 x 3/8, pointing to a small standoff near top right MP8 — jack, nylon, banana type, red MP9(3) — three of item MP9 (jack, nylon, banana type, black) MP10 — handle, aluminum, black, 6-32 (bottom right panel) H7(2) — two of item H7 (washer, plastic, #8) H6(2) — two of item H6 (screw, PHP, 6-32 x 3/8) MP4 — battery enclosure, bottom (lower left) BT1-BT4(4) — four gel-cell batteries, shown side by side in the main body of the assembly MP2 — battery enclosure, rear end H4(12) — twelve of item H4 (screw, PHP, 6-32 x 1/4) H1(4) — four of item H1 (nut, insulator) MP6 — battery panel w/switch (front panel, lower right, with switch and jacks mounted) H2(4) — four of item H2 (screw, thread forming), lower right edge, shown with a screw symbol Drawing numbers: 732A-1604 (inset), 732A-4004 (main view)",
