   "level": 2,
   "boards": [],
   "html": "<p>On page 8-5, Figure 8-2, delete J1,J2,J3 and J4 as shown in Figure 2.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Figure 2.<\/strong> (schematic — Battery PCB, 732A-1054)<br>Boxed \"BATTERY PCB\" / \"732A-1054\" containing: J4-P4 connector pins 1-6 wired to RT1 (10K, 25°C) and RT2 (10K, 25°C); BT1+, BT2+, BT3+, BT4+ cells each with BLK/RED leads to nodes E9, E10, E11, E12(E13), E14, E15, E16 (labels shown as E9○ E10, E12 E13○ E14, E15○ E16 per drawing — see below); node E4 (+) at left; R1 51K resistor; CR1 diode; DS1 lamp; nodes E3 (+RED), E1 (RED), E2 (BLK), E6, E5, E8, E7. To the right, outside the PCB box: S1 switch labeled \"BATTERY ON-OFF, ON/OFF\" with RED lead, and J10 connector pins 1/2 labeled \"POWER INPUT\".<br>Caption: Figure 2.<\/p>",
   "text": "On page 8-5, Figure 8-2, delete J1,J2,J3 and J4 as shown in Figure 2. Figure 2. (schematic — Battery PCB, 732A-1054) Boxed \"BATTERY PCB\" / \"732A-1054\" containing: J4-P4 connector pins 1-6 wired to RT1 (10K, 25°C) and RT2 (10K, 25°C); BT1+, BT2+, BT3+, BT4+ cells each with BLK/RED leads to nodes E9, E10, E11, E12(E13), E14, E15, E16 (labels shown as E9○ E10, E12 E13○ E14, E15○ E16 per drawing — see below); node E4 (+) at left; R1 51K resistor; CR1 diode; DS1 lamp; nodes E3 (+RED), E1 (RED), E2 (BLK), E6, E5, E8, E7. To the right, outside the PCB box: S1 switch labeled \"BATTERY ON-OFF, ON/OFF\" with RED lead, and J10 connector pins 1/2 labeled \"POWER INPUT\". Caption: Figure 2.",
