   "level": 3,
   "boards": [],
   "html": "<p>On page 3-2, add:<\/p>\n<p><strong>3-29. Overtemperature Protection<\/strong><br>3-30. Protection against overtemperature is provided by a 58 C thermal fuse (F2) which is placed directly on top of the ovenized reference module. When F2 opens, it interrupts the +18.6V supply connection to the oven heater. It also disconnects the +18.6V from the latch circuit Q6 on the Regulator PCB causing the IN CAL LED to go out and stay out until the fault is corrected.<\/p>\n<p>On page 3-3/3-4, Figure 3-1, add the thermal fuse (F2) as shown in Figure 5.<\/p>\n<p>On page 5-3, Table 5-1,<\/p>\n<p>ADD: F2| FUSE, THERMAL 58°C| 715110| 89536| 715110| 1<\/p>\n<p>On page 5-5, Table 5-1,<\/p>\n<p>CHANGE: RT1|...<br>TO: RT3,RT4|...<\/p>\n<p>On page 5-8, Figure 5-1 add F2 to the OVEN TOP VIEW as shown in Figure 6.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Figure 5.<\/strong> (block diagram)<br>Boxes: \"A4 REGULATOR / Q1,Q2,Q3,Q4\" feeding 18.5V dc through F2 to a dashed-line box labeled \"OVEN\" containing \"A5 REFERENCE / Q1,Q2,Q5,U1,U2,A4,Q12\" and \"HEATER\" (with a variable-resistor/thermistor symbol), and \"OUTPUT DIVIDER\". Outputs: A5 REFERENCE → 10V TERMINAL; OUTPUT DIVIDER → 1.018V TERMINAL and 1V TERMINAL.<br>Caption: Figure 5.<\/p>",
   "text": "On page 3-2, add: 3-29. Overtemperature Protection 3-30. Protection against overtemperature is provided by a 58 C thermal fuse (F2) which is placed directly on top of the ovenized reference module. When F2 opens, it interrupts the +18.6V supply connection to the oven heater. It also disconnects the +18.6V from the latch circuit Q6 on the Regulator PCB causing the IN CAL LED to go out and stay out until the fault is corrected. On page 3-3/3-4, Figure 3-1, add the thermal fuse (F2) as shown in Figure 5. On page 5-3, Table 5-1, ADD: F2| FUSE, THERMAL 58°C| 715110| 89536| 715110| 1 On page 5-5, Table 5-1, CHANGE: RT1|... TO: RT3,RT4|... On page 5-8, Figure 5-1 add F2 to the OVEN TOP VIEW as shown in Figure 6. Figure 5. (block diagram) Boxes: \"A4 REGULATOR / Q1,Q2,Q3,Q4\" feeding 18.5V dc through F2 to a dashed-line box labeled \"OVEN\" containing \"A5 REFERENCE / Q1,Q2,Q5,U1,U2,A4,Q12\" and \"HEATER\" (with a variable-resistor/thermistor symbol), and \"OUTPUT DIVIDER\". Outputs: A5 REFERENCE → 10V TERMINAL; OUTPUT DIVIDER → 1.018V TERMINAL and 1V TERMINAL. Caption: Figure 5.",
